<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israeli settler and Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09df011bd7cd05edb2321a0bccbf38d5b2521df921554abc28b6581dde9ec1ac</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T15:30:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--6ec13ca89571.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-israeli-settler-and-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">A suspected Palestinian gunman on Sunday shot dead an Israeli man near a West Bank settlement, according to Israeli officials. The gunman was located at a Ramallah hospital and arrested, police said. Elsewhere in the West Bank, Israeli soldiers killed a Palestinian motorist who the military said was attempting to run them over. The flare up in violence came on the eve of the Jewish holy day of Yom Kippur.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>An Israeli settler and a Palestinian driver killed in West Bank shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:549cf6d2dd407191de6320c9f5275cab1b042df03692e0bed99e9423ead1c6cf</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:34:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings--7750aafd0f5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/an-israeli-settler-and-a-palestinian-driver-killed-in-west-bank-shootings" /><summary type="html">An Israeli settler has been fatally shot in the occupied West Bank, while Israel's military said it killed a man who attempted to ram his vehicle into troops elsewhere in the Palestinian territory. The news came as violence in the West Bank is escalating at a very rapid pace. “All Israeli military authorities involved with the West Bank have been warning the Israeli government that the situation is basically out of control”, explains FRANCE 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran closes French language centre in Tehran for ‘illegal acts’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a4e3814d30b50a9972622a1b713d5f650ccdb6c1498dd1d9415d014ab36d5e7</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts--e9366397fe37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-iran-closes-french-language-centre-in-tehran-for-illegal-acts" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities on Sunday shut down the French Language Centre (CLF) in Tehran, alleging the French embassy-linked institute conducted "illegal acts that violated diplomatic conventions" and "abused its status as a language training facility". France has vowed to take "appropriate measures" in response.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Syria protests, Céline Dion on stage and Quito wildfires</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93c0939360e19a7a8413517b67a0827e2b4867334d3f5a1065ab82dc0abd1118</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:15:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c_line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires--7c494f9fc87e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260920-the-week-in-pictures-syria-protests-c%C3%A9line-dion-on-stage-and-quito-wildfires" /><summary type="html">From protests against rising fuel prices in Syria to Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney’s EU charm offensive to Quito’s wildfires and Céline Dion’s return to the stage, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks and no Western support: What are Saudi Arabia's options ?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94d5d878dc4899e6b5db3454415b4a44728a29c32e5d75f82eba407e1ca97d84</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:24:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options--12b32e145452.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthi-attacks-and-no-western-support-what-are-saudi-arabia-s-options" /><summary type="html">The US has warned that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthis could rapidly escalate. It comes after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The Houthis' lightning offensive seized swathes of Yemeni territory in recent weeks and has left hundreds dead. In the face of such attacks and with no support from its American ally, what are Saudi Arabia’s options?</summary></entry><entry><title>'NAZA' documentary about Gaza war sparks political storm in Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25153b7a0bf0a2a1093f9e97647f0106e0b24dc031ca9e5a43b092c6d467a631</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:22:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel--e9ca19249009.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/naza-documentary-about-gaza-war-sparks-political-storm-in-israel" /><summary type="html">The Israeli filmmakers behind the documentary NAZA may have received a standing ovation at the Venice film festival, they have been facing violent threats to their lives and citizenship at home in Israel. A month ahead of crucial elections, the film profiles anonymous military sources who speak about the widespread killing of civilians in Gaza. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said he intends to introduce legislation aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers". Details by Shirli Sitbon, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why doesn't the US intervene to defend Saudi Arabia against the Houthis?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7f384f683c281243d439d94f4d61f9bbe754f27e9064c35241cbfdb1ba87cf</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T12:20:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis--e9d56b00d69a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/why-doesn-t-the-us-intervene-to-defend-saudi-arabia-against-the-houthis" /><summary type="html">The US cautioned against a rapidly escalating situation in Yemen after Houthi rebels carried out a missile attack on the Saudi capital. In recent weeks, the Iran backed militants have also seized large portions of Yemeni territory following clashes with Saudi-backed government forces. The US is a very close ally to Saudi Arabia. Yet, is visibly unwilling to intervene on its behalf – why? Details and analysis by H. A. Hellyer, senior fellow in geopolitics at the Royal United Institute in Cairo.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis strike Saudi capital Riyadh for the first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8df039f2ad73be615889fecc8fb1d22492de6c2820c250254ff62a80b07c670d</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T09:38:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time--3eef0d6b1feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-strike-saudi-capital-riyadh-for-the-first-time" /><summary type="html">Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Saudi Arabia continues to intensify. On Saturday morning, a fire broke out near Riyadh's main airport after Houthis said they launched missiles and drones at Saudi Arabia. On the ground in Yemen, Houthi rebels are pushing east in their fight against Saudi-backed government forces. Story by Caroline Baum.</summary></entry><entry><title>Black smoke seen near Riyadh amid air raid alerts in Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f481ce1a7f1225c2fa8400fbe5630eafab0e95017d44c8d918b8cb032f788bc</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:16:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia--6a862c3c701b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/black-smoke-seen-near-riyadh-amid-air-raid-alerts-in-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">⁠Flames and plumes of smoke ‌were ⁠seen ‌rising near ⁠Riyadh airport this afternoon with flights cancelled and delayed. This as fighting between Saudi-backed government forces and Iran-backed Houthi rebels has killed 48 people in recent hours. The rebels staged a lightning offensive this month, seizing swathes of territory in Yemen and launching a barrage of missiles and drones toward Saudi Arabia. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Jamie Smith-Maillet.</summary></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia says air defences intercepted Houthi ballistic missile targeting Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:222f01e388436c18ea306e8ea62c7ef5ff5ee07b5f896044c99fba51c4aa9911</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:53:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported--d192137a4871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-smoke-flames-seen-near-riyadh-airport-major-flight-disruptions-reported" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia on Saturday confirmed that Yemen’s Houthi rebels tried to attack its capital with a ballistic missile, the first targeting of Riyadh since the escalation in fighting with the rebels. The confirmation came hours after the Houthis said they targeted "sensitive sites" in Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: 'NAZA' documentary sparks political storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e151a23074908c6294dfa489adbcb06aaac9205c822fba549d9bd989e1059dde</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T12:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm--19a457356dcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260919-israel-naza-documentary-sparks-political-storm" /><summary type="html">The documentary film 'NAZA', and its co-directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor, are at the centre of a controversy in Israel.The film, which won an award at the Venice Film Festival, features anonymous Israeli sources accusing the military of intentionally killing numerous civilians in Gaza.Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Wednesday that he intended to "strip of their citizenship" those who "defame" the Israeli army.</summary></entry><entry><title>US fears wider Middle East escalation after Houthis attack Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e48634114a59f42d959aa2604a84ddcab392528c4b83055dd2f03cfe5fb8651e</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-us-fears-rapid-escalation-in-mideast-after-houthis-attack-riyadh--2e2fa664288a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260919-us-fears-rapid-escalation-in-mideast-after-houthis-attack-riyadh" /><summary type="html">The United States warned Saturday that fighting between Saudi Arabia and Iran-backed Houthi forces could “escalate rapidly” after a missile attack targeted Riyadh for the first time since the Yemen conflict resumed. The attack prompted US President Donald Trump to cut short a weekend at a secluded presidential complex in rural Maryland and return to the White House.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>More than 112,000 displaced in Yemen as Houthis seize more ground</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2ccdb0f2f0a9c132ae86355a6316ccbbcc1a02ab3d2ec0eb911d5728898ed71</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:57:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground--fdb60ca50a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/more-than-112-000-displaced-in-yemen-as-houthis-seize-more-ground" /><summary type="html">Pro-Houthi demonstrations erupted in Yemen after Saudi Arabia accused the military group of targeting the Muslim holy site of Mecca. Story by Elitsa Gadeva.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI: Silicon Species or Trojan Horse? Riyadh Calling, Russia Votes &amp; the Ed Sheeran debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:526eeaa8b12dbcdfc8c0808def4c7c1801d9d7d66825a3b1b7f8a6abc77e92da</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260918-time-to-stop-suggesting-ai-is-conscious-riyadh-calling-saudi-s-hour-of-news-russian-electio--1626fef711b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260918-time-to-stop-suggesting-ai-is-conscious-riyadh-calling-saudi-s-hour-of-news-russian-elections" /><summary type="html">This week, Saudi Arabia has turned to its allies for military support as Iran-backed Houthi rebels tighten their grip on Yemen’s Red Sea coast and the Bab el Mandeb shipping choke point, while drone attacks on the Kingdom’s oil infrastructure deepen an emerging energy crisis. In Russia, voters head to the polls for a tightly controlled parliamentary election with little meaningful opposition, as Putin insists there will be no new mobilisation. Meanwhile, warnings about the risks of AI are coming from inside the industry itself, with Microsoft AI chief Mustafa Suleyman warning against treating AI models like humans—and raising the prospect of a new “silicon species” competing with us for resources. Finally, in Britain, the royal family is back on the defensive as Earl Spencer’s new claims about Princess Diana’s funeral prompt an unusually pointed response from Buckingham Palace.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>US approves $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 warplanes to Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24803ef4fcc4c8af1752809c8d5709ae6cfb017532006015fba3c4515e1f562d</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:29:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260918-us-approves-24-3-billion-sale-of-48-f-35-warplanes-to-saudi-arabia--beccdf59d388.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260918-us-approves-24-3-billion-sale-of-48-f-35-warplanes-to-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">The United States on Thursday said it had approved a $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 stealth warplanes to Saudi Arabia. Israel has previously voiced concerns about Riyadh buying F-35s, despite a push to normalise relations.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump declines to back Saudi Arabia as US officials reportedly meet Iran-backed Houthis in Oman</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5886f8bced3160feb39b621226fd5cb5df9852117eeaa22f1a4b4abe8f87444e</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T18:47:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-declines-to-back-saudi-arabia-as-us-officials-reportedly-meet-iran-backed-houthis-in-oman--ac26297dddfb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-declines-to-back-saudi-arabia-as-us-officials-reportedly-meet-iran-backed-houthis-in-oman" /><summary type="html">US officials met representatives of Yemen's Houthis in Oman over the weekend, five sources familiar with the matter said, days after the Iran-backed militia seized a strategic ​stretch of the ‌Red Sea coast in a sweeping offensive that routed Saudi-backed forces. U.S. ​President Donald Trump has so far rebuffed pleas from the Saudis for military support fighting the Houthis. FRANCE 24's Fraser Jackson reports from Washington.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Stalemate' in Lebanon: Hezbollah justifies weapons, citing Israeli occupation and ongoing attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0627b3f9a3f272f923bf58a643bdbc592b3cd085402eda0761ecb36db4a7df4d</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T18:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/stalemate-in-lebanon-hezbollah-justifies-weapons-citing-israeli-occupation-and-ongoing-attacks--48baabef35de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/stalemate-in-lebanon-hezbollah-justifies-weapons-citing-israeli-occupation-and-ongoing-attacks" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr Filippo Dionigi, Senior Lecturer in Politics and International Relations at the University of Bristol. According to Dr. Dionigi, the central obstacle to Hezbollah’s disarmament is not simply the military capacity of the Lebanese state, but the absence of a political settlement capable of making disarmament both legitimate and sustainable. While additional funding and weapons would strengthen the Lebanese Armed Forces, they will not resolve the fundamental political dilemma.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Sanctions won’t prevent us from doing our job' says ICC Prosecutor Mame Mandiaye Niang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cadd9d6901047cecc6b212dc1d5a22b39cff67577d817c14680bf4b309da1621</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260917-sanctions-won-t-prevent-us-from-doing-our-job-says-icc-prosecutor-mame-mandiaye-niang--ed22f3ec8e7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20260917-sanctions-won-t-prevent-us-from-doing-our-job-says-icc-prosecutor-mame-mandiaye-niang" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, the acting Prosecutor of the International Criminal Court tells FRANCE 24 that the court is needed now more than ever to ensure there is no gap for impunity. Mame Mandiaye Niang says the court’s job is to step in if domestic justice systems fail. The Senegalese judge is at the centre of a storm amid sanctions put on the court by the US after its issuing of arrest warrants for Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and former Defence Minister Yoav Gallant over Israel’s actions in Gaza. He explained how the sanctions affect his daily life but says it won’t stop the court doing its job.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza documentary 'NAZA' sparks political storm, threats against directors in Israel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4121a1d708860f65ca7aa2a4b9f77f743289a6d0e418e8c897afaa3d1bcf99a9</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T15:24:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-gaza-documentary-naza-sparks-political-storm-in-israel--296179ca2a75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-gaza-documentary-naza-sparks-political-storm-in-israel" /><summary type="html">The award-winning documentary "NAZA" featuring anonymous military sources speaking about Israel's mass killing of civilians in Gaza has sparked a political firestorm in Israel. The film's directors and their families have received a wave of threats, while Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu announced a plan for a bill aimed at revoking the citizenship of people who "defame IDF soldiers".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Amnesty accuses Iran of crimes against humanity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92955f9af708214f59dcd0befa87dc22508fe8594901b55457508395dba42b43</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:55:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/amnesty-accuses-iran-of-crimes-against-humanity--a095e69f4f2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/amnesty-accuses-iran-of-crimes-against-humanity" /><summary type="html">Amnesty International has accused Iranian authorities of committing crimes against humanity during the 2022 Woman, Life, Freedom crackdown, saying more than 500 people, including 71 children, were killed and that the violence disproportionately targeted Kurdish and Baluchi communities. The rights group is urging the UN General Assembly to create an international justice mechanism, arguing that many of the officials it identified remain in positions of power.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim Saudi F-15 kill as Yemen fighting escalates</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1e6092ec92783789bbcf50eaa5d534a9e31827112a2e03eb50b19ccc7dcffd</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthis-claim-saudi-f-15-kill-as-yemen-fighting-escalates--1c07fa3889e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-claim-saudi-f-15-kill-as-yemen-fighting-escalates" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthi rebels have released footage they say shows the wreckage of a Saudi F-15 fighter jet, which, if confirmed, would mark the first fighter jet they have shot down. The claim comes as fighting escalates in Yemen, with the Houthis expanding their control around the strategic Bab al-Mandab Strait and the UN urging both sides to return to negotiations.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon on Paris talks : 'the general sentiment here is very little hope'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b956b189bdcf8bdc2b4ce3defc24555c7979a7c211ad5305d60194d2d8da882c</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:46:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-on-paris-talks-the-general-sentiment-here-is-very-little-hope--c99b6c38243c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-on-paris-talks-the-general-sentiment-here-is-very-little-hope" /><summary type="html">Lebanese President Joseph Aoun is in Paris for talks with Emmanuel Macron, but on the ground many Lebanese say they have little hope after months of war with Israel, the continued occupation of parts of southern Lebanon and uncertainty over regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Renée David reports from Beirut on hopes that Aoun and Macron can rally international backing and secure a framework agreement to help stabilise the country.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: UNIFIL withdrawal at the heart of Paris talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08ec2fead56f651f580ed0d98e67f0a9637eefa202519cbc724573c573deced7</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:23:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks--35b3812f5e58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-unifil-withdrawal-at-the-heart-of-paris-talks" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron welcomes Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II to Paris today for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as France pushes to prevent a security vacuum ahead of UNIFIL's planned withdrawal at the end of 2026, with Israeli strikes continuing in southern Lebanon and concerns growing over who will secure the border. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Syrian court issues first sentences over 2025 massacres of Alawites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:033b75500f8072ce9d2166d6814a2dcfd395256cd4391b37b431f47b9afbb327</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:13:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-syrian-court-issues-first-sentences-over-2025-massacres-of-alawites--523981634efd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-syrian-court-issues-first-sentences-over-2025-massacres-of-alawites" /><summary type="html">Syria's judiciary on Thursday issued its first verdicts over the massacres of Alawites on the Syrian coast last year, sentencing a former member of government forces to 20 years in prison. A supporter of deposed president Bashar al-Assad received a death sentence and another was sentenced to life in jail.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: Emmanuel Macron welcomes Joseph Aoun to Paris for Middle East talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6252b0841aacf1811203cc104717317dbd444ba2266a3884669a0c4807d8ce17</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:48:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-emmanuel-macron-welcomes-joseph-aoun-to-paris-for-middle-east-talks--f7c6701a6630.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-emmanuel-macron-welcomes-joseph-aoun-to-paris-for-middle-east-talks" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun in Paris for talks focused on Lebanon's security and wider Middle East tensions, with Jordan's King Abdullah II also taking part in the meeting. FRANCE 24's Luke Shrago and Kethevane Gorjestani have the analysis from Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lebanon: Macron, Aoun and King Abdullah II hold security talks in Paris</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eef3f6d293b3c0188f6e7cddb021cd282fbc3b367a8c308b74c722a8f3dd5649</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:59:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lebanon-macron-aoun-and-king-abdullah-ii-hold-security-talks-in-paris--7db26b0f193d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lebanon-macron-aoun-and-king-abdullah-ii-hold-security-talks-in-paris" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron is hosting Lebanese President Joseph Aoun and Jordan's King Abdullah II in Paris for talks on Lebanon's security and international support for the Lebanese army. The meeting comes as concerns grow over Israel's continued strikes in southern Lebanon and the possible end of the UNIFIL peacekeeping mission, with France seeking a "clear, credible and realistic" plan to back Lebanon through funding, equipment and military training.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East : Trump plans $2.8bn arms package for Israel amid Gaza war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7edb0ca3c6d783089083a9b52953485823e8f25bc512ea775d83c4011ed72c2b</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:55:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-trump-plans-2-8bn-arms-package-for-israel-amid-gaza-war--7162074c4801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-trump-plans-2-8bn-arms-package-for-israel-amid-gaza-war" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration is reportedly preparing a $2.8 billion arms package for Israel, including 40,000 bombs, as Israel continues strikes in Gaza despite last October's ceasefire. The proposed deal would further strengthen Israel's military capabilities and revive deliveries of 2,000-pound bombs that had previously been paused over concerns about civilian casualties.</summary></entry><entry><title>US allows Iranian delegation to attend UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:030aff4915b4487f3d508e382323fcb19b04c520eda1ab83891edd1096fbd988</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T06:14:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-middle-east-live-paris-talks-lebanese-army-unifil-israel-iran-yemen--232433616bca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-middle-east-live-paris-talks-lebanese-army-unifil-israel-iran-yemen" /><summary type="html">The US State Department said Thursday it had approved visas for top Iranian officials, including President Masoud Pezeshkian and Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi, to attend next week’s UN General Assembly in New York. The delegation will be smaller than last year and will face some travel restrictions. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel and Morocco agree to open embassies after New York talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36f398bec45872932c0dfcf7c2f80302f282473e8ff70566c75f23cd7bec82d5</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T01:07:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-israel-morocco-embassies-new-york--18d04519b87c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260917-israel-morocco-embassies-new-york" /><summary type="html">Israel and Morocco agreed on Wednesday to open embassies in each other’s countries following talks between their foreign ministers and the US ambassador to the United Nations in New York. The two countries established diplomatic ties in 2020 under the US-brokered Abraham Accords, which normalised Israel’s relations with several Arab states.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran's tour in trouble after opening acts drop out in solidarity with rapper Macklemore</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ab8cc05dbe8ad4fcb31a53b3393b73c09874f37cbaf162ede260c39261827ba</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T21:33:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-opening-acts-drop-out-in-solidarity-with-rapper-macklemo--d0535056d660.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260916-ed-sheeran-s-tour-in-trouble-after-opening-acts-drop-out-in-solidarity-with-rapper-macklemore" /><summary type="html">Ed Sheeran's tour of North and South America has been roiled by the decision this week to drop Macklemore as an opener because of the rapper's onstage pro-Palestinian comments. Since then, all of Sheeran's other supporting acts have dropped out, including a group that backs Sheeran up during part of the show. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with David Jackson, Professor of Political Science at Bowling Green State University about the issue.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry></feed>
